      <div type="clause" n="6.3">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:ICn">I Cn</ref> 6.3</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="290" ed="#liebermann"/>And æghwylc<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.3"/> Cristen mann<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.4"/> eac<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.5"/> for his Drihtenes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.6"/> ege unrihthæmed georne forbuge ⁊ godcunde lage rihtlice healde.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.7"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.3" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="290" ed="#liebermann"/>And æghwylc Cristen man eac for<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.1"/> his Drihtnes ege unrihthamed georne forbuge ⁊ godcunda lage rihtlice healdæn.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="6.3" corresp="#wit-d-frags"><pb n="290" ed="#liebermann"/>And æghwilc Cristen man eac for his Drihtenes ege unrihthæmed georne forbuge ⁊ godcunde laga rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.3" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="290" ed="#liebermann"/>Et omnis Christianus pro timore sui Creatoris iniustum concubitum uitet et Dei<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.oe.6-2"/> legem teneat.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.3" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="291" ed="#liebermann"/>Omnem etiam Christianum obnixe precamur, fornicationem deuitare, leges et praecepta Dei diligenter custodire.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="6.3" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="291" ed="#liebermann"/>Omnis etiam Christianus pro timore Domini iniustum coitum diligenter uitet et diuinam legem recte custodiat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="6a.3" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="162" ed="#robertson"/>And æghwylc Cristen mann eac for his Drihtenes ege unrihthæmed georne forbuge ⁊ godcunde lage rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="240" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And æghwylc Cristen mann eac for his Drihtenes ege unrihthæmed georne forbuge and godcunde lage rihtlice healde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="291" ed="#liebermann"/>Und auch jeder [andere] Christenmensch meide aus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.de.1"/> Furcht vor seinem Herr[gott] willig gesetzwidrigen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#ICn_6-3.lnote.de.2"/> Beischlaf und halte gesetzlich geistliche Rechtsordnung(en?).</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every [other] Christian man also, for fear of his Lord, eagerly avoid unlawful intercourse and keep the law(s?) of God rightly.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-g-a"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#ICn_6-3.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="163" ed="#robertson"/>All Christian men likewise through the fear of God<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#ICn_6-3.robnote.n.2"/> shall strictly avoid illicit unions<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#ICn_6-3.robnote.n.3"/> and duly observe the laws of the church.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="241" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And for fear of God, every Christian must diligently avoid unlawful intercourse and rightly uphold the divine law.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="291"><ref target="clause:VAtr_10">V Atr 10</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 10</note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:VIAtr_11">VI Atr 11</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 6:3: Cn 1018 11:3  VI Atr 11</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="356"><label>quoted verbatim (bold in Wormald's table)</label> <ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-024">Cn 1018 11.3</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, I Cn 6:3: Cn 1018 11:3  VI Atr 11</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="346"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-024">Cn 1018 11.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#kennedy" n="59"><ref target="clause:Cn-1018_part-024">Cn 1018 11.3–12.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="373"><ref target="clause:Ymb-Aewbricas_Not-known-to-Liebermann">Ymb Æwbricas</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares V Atr 10.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 291, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
